{# Did this article help?

   Two submit buttons in a real form, so it works with no scripting: the post
   goes to /ajax/article-vote, which answers a browser with a redirect back
   here and answers fetch with JSON. Both hidden fields are carried for the
   same reason the subscribe form carries them -- without a script there is no
   header to put the token in, and no other way to say which page to return to.

   The chosen button stays enabled after a vote. The endpoint upserts on
   (slug, voter), so changing your mind is supported, and a block that locked
   itself would be hiding a thing the table can do. What marks the choice is a
   modifier class and the line above it, not `aria-pressed` -- these are
   submits, not toggles.

   The tally is printed only when `verdict.shown` says so. Below that it is one
   or two people, and "100% helpful" over a single vote is a claim rather than
   a figure. #}
{# Two callers now: a help article asking whether it answered the question, and
   an Airside post asking whether it was worth reading. Everything but the copy
   and the form's action is the same, so they share this rather than fork it --
   including the section id, which is what the endpoint's redirect lands on,
   and the `js-article-vote` hook, which the script finds by class and drives
   entirely from `form.action`. #}
{% set notice = article_vote_notice() %}
{# Every name here is prefixed, and that is not tidiness. The first version
   read `title|default(...)`, and `title` already exists in an article's
   context -- so the heading asking whether the page helped became the word
   "Baggage". A partial that takes options has to take them under names the
   page cannot already be using. #}
{% set vote_action = vote_action|default('/ajax/article-vote') %}
{% set vote_title = vote_title|default('Did this answer it, or are you still stuck?') %}
{% set vote_yes = vote_yes|default('Yes, this answered it') %}
{% set vote_no = vote_no|default('No, still stuck') %}
{% set vote_said_yes = vote_said_yes|default('You said this sorted it.') %}
{% set vote_said_no = vote_said_no|default('You said you were still stuck.') %}
{% set vote_tally = vote_tally|default('%yes% of %votes% readers found this helpful') %}
<section class="article__verdict" id="article-verdict" aria-labelledby="article-verdict-title">
    <div class="article__verdict-ask">
        <h2 class="article__verdict-title" id="article-verdict-title">{{ vote_title }}</h2>

        <p class="article__verdict-status js-vote-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"
           {% if notice %}data-tone="{{ notice.tone }}"{% endif %}>
            {%- if notice -%}
                {{ notice.message }}
            {%- elseif verdict.mine is same as(true) -%}
                {{ vote_said_yes }}
            {%- elseif verdict.mine is same as(false) -%}
                {{ vote_said_no }}
            {%- endif -%}
        </p>

        {# Spelled once. The script fills the same pattern off the data
           attribute after a vote, so the sentence a reader sees before and
           after cannot drift apart -- the reason the cookie notice and the
           currency switcher take their names off data attributes too. #}
        {% set tally = vote_tally %}
        <p class="article__verdict-tally js-vote-tally" data-template="{{ tally }}"
           {{- verdict.shown ? '' : ' hidden' }}>
            {{- verdict.shown ? tally|replace({'%yes%': verdict.yes, '%votes%': verdict.votes}) : '' -}}
        </p>
    </div>

    <form class="article__verdict-form js-article-vote" action="{{ vote_action }}" method="post">
        <input type="hidden" name="{{ csrf_field() }}" value="{{ csrf_token() }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="return_to" value="{{ current_page() }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="slug" value="{{ verdict.slug }}">

        <button type="submit" name="helpful" value="1"
                class="article__verdict-button article__verdict-button--up js-vote-yes{{ verdict.mine is same as(true) ? ' article__verdict-button--chosen' : '' }}"
                aria-label="{{ vote_yes }}">
            <i class="fas fa-thumbs-up" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </button>

        <button type="submit" name="helpful" value="0"
                class="article__verdict-button article__verdict-button--down js-vote-no{{ verdict.mine is same as(false) ? ' article__verdict-button--chosen' : '' }}"
                aria-label="{{ vote_no }}">
            <i class="fas fa-thumbs-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </button>
    </form>
</section>
